  "evidence_notes": [
    "Code snapshots establish configured behavior, not proof of every historical execution setting.",
    "Scaling dimensions and optimizer settings cross-checked with bundled plot_data/parameter_scaling_results.csv.",
    "Published m5.1 architecture cross-checked with the release manifest; stored float32 does not imply float32 training computation.",
    "Training accounting uses batch sequences times 256 model-input tokens, including BOS; dataset counts use 255 nucleotide tokens.",
    "The release manifest labels 166018940928 as nucleotide tokens, but its accounting and the training code use 256 tokens per example. Preserve it only as approximate model-input-token exposure.",
    "Early registered checkpoint steps do not establish the full run duration or every checkpoint used in manuscript plots.",
    "Cache suffix -5149 refers to the BOS-token cache rebuild issue https://github.com/marin-community/marin/issues/5149; corrected source alone does not verify all historical caches.",
    "Scaling CSV parameter counts are the configured estimator values, not tensor recounts: its 1B entry is 1120767360 versus 1120772224 in the released checkpoint. The difference is 4864 = 2 * 128 * 19, consistent with query/key normalization weights.",
    "The early proportional mixture used raw sequence counts, giving upstream fraction 0.1064416781; 10/90 is a rounded figure label.",
    "The direct early mixture comparison uses shared steps through 22000; the specialist bar comparison uses upstream step22000 and CDS step34000.",
    "Later mixture loader clamps requested slices to the available dataset and restarts exhausted components. The older scaling snapshot does not establish this later loader behavior.",
    "Offline lineage plots compose inherited stage fractions and preserve the first control checkpoint beyond the m5.1 endpoint. They omit the step29579 three-region checkpoint in the m5.1 curve and do not smooth scores.",
    "Displayed lineage-token totals use approximate inherited fractions of run token tags; they are not exact counters of unique bases or identical checkpoint horizons."
  ],
